      "I've spent the last few days building UI elements like visualizations, log explorers, chat support, profile viewers, and more. But my gut is telling me to take a step back and…",
    author: 'Cody Bontecou',
    markdown:
      "I've spent the last few days building UI elements like visualizations, log explorers, chat support, profile viewers, and more. But my gut is telling me to take a step back and strip it all out, realigning with the \"bridge\" idea, where the app is purely a bridge to connect users’ data to their AI agents.\n\nThe app should get out of the way, it's only there to help users get their data off their device. The real UI is the chat window they're already familiar with - ChatGPT, Claude, Grok, Pi.\n\nI'm not quite comfortable with the idea of \"my ideal customer is an AI agent\" but from everything I'm reading online, this seems to be the direction software and the market are heading. I think it might be smart to re-align and revert the last few days of work to niche down and focus on that idea.\n\nVisualizations, support bot, logs, etc. only create more code for our agents to navigate through, more surface area for bugs, and more feature requests and extensions in the future.\n\nI think isobot still has a place in this app, but maybe it's best to leave it out for the MVP. At least the customer-facing aspect of it. I still want it in the background monitoring support questions, tickets, and first passes on bug and feature requests.",
